text: <|channel|>analysis<|message|>We need to explain the process: yeast ferments sugars producing CO2 and alcohol, CO2 gets trapped in dough, causing rise. Also yeast metabolism, gluten network, etc. Provide details: yeast is a microorganism, Saccharomyces cerevisiae, metabolizes sugars via glycolysis, produces CO2 and ethanol. The CO2 expands, dough rises. Also yeast also produces other compounds that contribute to flavor. The gluten network traps gas. Also the dough is elastic, so it can hold gas. Also the yeast also produces heat, but main is CO2. Also the yeast's metabolism is anaerobic in dough. Also the dough's temperature and hydration affect yeast activity. Also the yeast's growth and reproduction. Also the yeast's ability to produce CO2 is due to fermentation. Also the dough's gluten network forms a matrix that traps gas. Also the yeast's metabolism is influenced by sugar concentration, pH, temperature. Also the yeast's ability to produce CO
